      "value": "@{5f2e2ab863aa6f7311d53d03|full_name}: I mean the context is not all that important, but if you run at it head-on in a world with fast movement, you run through the area where the confirm is very quickly, the distance for it is very small, you have to pretty much have your face in the blue to get the prompt.  If i run at it i have to spam my trigger to be sure it goes through instead of just able to click once.  The delayed reaction doesn't help.  I'm sure a lot of people find themselves having to click many times or stop and wait to make sure.  It's just not a smooth action.  I personally have had it happen where i was clicking and it didn't actually hit it despite me mashing while i was running, forcing me to turn around and try again by deliberately moving to the centre of it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
